    "result_text": "All 254 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` household-joining feature for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, an owner whose `lastName` + `address` match an existing owner is now allowed (instead of being rejected 409), and both the new owner and the matched existing owner(s) are assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New pipeline step** `AssignOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 runs inside the create transaction after the duplicate check. When `sharesHousehold` is true, it finds existing owners with the same normalized `lastName`+`address` (same normalization rule as `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold`), derives a stable `HH-<hex>` id from those fields (reusing an existing member's id if one already has it), and assigns it to the new owner and each matched existing owner (persisting the existing ones). No-ops otherwise.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHousehold` between `rejectHousehold` and `assignCustomerCode`, governed by `transaction` so it commits with the new owner's save.\n\n3. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema, so it's mapped into `OwnerDto` and returned by both create and GET.\n\n5. **Schemas** \u2014 added a `household_id` column to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files, and a trailing `NULL` to the positional owners seed rows in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (the profile the tests use; h2/mysql/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe existing `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold` already short-circuits when `sharesHousehold` is true, so the reject path is unchanged for the opt-out case.",
